 98%", "Polls show Little leading by 10-21 points with fragmented opposition"], "rationale": "Brad Little benefits from Idaho's strong Republican tilt, incumbency, and a fragmented opposition including independent, Libertarian, and Constitution Party candidates splitting non-Republican votes. Every expert rater calls the race Safe or Solid R, and both prediction markets price a Little win at 97-98%, consistent with polls showing him well ahead.", "watch": "A surprise consolidation of the non-Republican field behind one challenger, or a scandal involving Little, could tighten the race, though even then the state's partisan lean makes an upset very unlikely.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Brad Little (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Idaho's governor race is among the least competitive in the country this cycle. Republican incumbent Brad Little, first elected in 2018 and reelected in 2022, seeks a third term in a state that leans about 18 points Republican. He faces Democrat Terri Pickens along with an independent, a Libertarian, and a Constitution Party candidate, meaning the non-Republican vote is split several ways.\n\nPolling from September shows Little ahead by double digits, and both major prediction markets give him roughly a 97-98 percent chance of winning. All seven expert raters place the race in the Safe or Solid Republican column. Republicans also hold the fundraising advantage across Idaho's statewide races. The main open question is the size of Little's winning margin rather than the outcome itself.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0111, "margin": -14.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0115, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0087, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0158, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0168, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0122, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.015, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem"